Subject: [PATCH 12/57] fix-data-3: MR-28 minimums, shift-inclusive and
 part-time hourly figures leave the base-pay cells; one Juice line

scripts/build-market.js notBasePay: a stated minimum, an hourly figure that includes the highest shift
differential and part-time hourly pay at 2,080 hours enter no market cell and are counted on the company entry
(minimum, shiftPay, partTime). The drawer's Juice block says 'Gross pay is the posted minimum.' or 'Gross pay
includes the top shift differential.' in one line. MR-28 is a real test now in beta-methodology-2.

